From 6676ed7197c1508381846103a746d62020e7e786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:07:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Chapter3 AI: ask about any home, one look for every AI
 feature, and the rental analyzer inside the rental guide

- Listing pages: Ask about this home. A signed-up visitor asks anything; Chapter3 AI answers from that listing's facts and description only, through the AI proxy, and never gives a value, a rate or a payment. Not signed up: the sign-up, as for the description.
- One look for every AI feature (idx-lib/ai.js): the Chapter3 AI chip, a navy chip with a brass sparkle, on the AI search box, the AI picks on the map, the rental analyzer's overview and the new chat.
- /invest/long-term-rental/: ?embed=1 shows only the analyzer, for a guide page that frames it, and reports its height.
- /invest/run-the-numbers/: the real rental analyzer in place of the page's calculator; the 1 percent count says the day it ran, from the data; a hard offer to run the count again and send every house that passes.
- tools/idx-test.mjs: two controls for the chat (facts only for a signed-up visitor, never as markup).
