 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is a good DSCR for a Myrtle Beach rental?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A DSCR of 1.0 means the rent exactly covers the payment. Most DSCR lenders want to see 1.1 to 1.25, and pricing improves meaningfully above 1.25. Below 1.0, expect a larger down payment or a lower offer price to make the deal work."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How much down payment do investment loans require?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Plan on a much larger down payment than an owner-occupied loan for conventional and DSCR investment loans. Non-warrantable condos and condotels often require more, and putting more down generally buys a better rate."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is a condotel, and can it be financed?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A condotel is a condo building run with hotel-style operations: a front desk, nightly stays, and an onsite rental program. They fall outside standard lending guidelines, so financing comes from specialty and portfolio lenders at higher down payments. That is why many condotel units trade in cash."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Are HOA fees a deal-breaker for condo investing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Judge the net, not the fee. Many oceanfront HOA fees bundle building insurance, water, cable, pest control, and exterior maintenance, costs a single-family landlord pays separately. A unit with a $650 fee that covers insurance can out-earn a cheaper-fee building that covers nothing."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What taxes surprise new Horry County investors?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Three usually surprise people. Rental property is assessed at the 6 percent rate rather than the 4 percent owner-occupied rate. The county levies personal property tax on the furnishings inside a rental. Short stays trigger state and local accommodations taxes on top of income tax."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What insurance does a coastal rental need?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Wind and hail coverage with a percentage deductible, flood coverage priced by zone, and for condos an HO-6 policy sized to fill the gaps in the building's master policy. Quotes vary widely street to street, so price insurance during due diligence, not after."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which areas lease fastest for long-term tenants?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Carolina Forest, Conway, Socastee, and Market Common consistently show deep tenant pools because demand comes from the year-round workforce, schools, the hospital systems, and Coastal Carolina University rather than tourism."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need a business license to rent out property?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Generally yes. The City of Myrtle Beach and Horry County both require rental business licenses, and short-term rentals can need additional permits depending on the municipality. HOAs often require registration on top of that."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What does property management cost here?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Long-term management typically runs 8 to 10 percent of collected rent plus a leasing fee. Full-service short-term management runs 20 to 30 percent of revenue, with cleaning billed to guests or owners depending on the operator."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What vacancy should I use?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Use 5 to 8 percent for a long-term rental as a planning number, and budget separately for turn costs like paint and carpet between tenants. Furnished monthly rentals run different math because winter tenants book in blocks."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do nearby construction permits matter?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, in both directions. Clusters of renovation permits usually mark improving streets, while heavy new-unit construction nearby can cap rent growth. This analyzer pulls recent Horry County permit activity around the address automatically so the signal is in front of you."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Should I pay cash or finance?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Borrowed money can help or hurt: financing raises cash-on-cash return when the spread between rent yield and rate is positive, and lowers it when the spread is negative. A common Grand Strand path is closing with a DSCR loan, then refinancing after rents season or renovations raise value. Cash still wins for speed and for condotels."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I still invest here if my property can’t be a short-term rental?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, and this is one of the most useful workarounds on the Grand Strand. Many Myrtle Beach residential zones (and plenty of HOAs) don’t allow Airbnb-style short-term rentals. South Carolina’s 90-day threshold is a tax rule: stays under 90 days are subject to the state accommodations tax. It does not override local zoning. Cities, counties and HOAs set their own minimum lease terms, and those minimums vary, so a 90-day lease is not automatically permitted where nightly rentals are banned. Mid-term tenants such as traveling nurses, remote workers and October-to-March snowbirds are a common way to cash-flow a property in those zones. Before you count on it, confirm the minimum lease term in that city’s ordinance and the HOA covenants for the specific address. Run any address through the analyzer to compare the long-term and mid-term numbers."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What does the long-term rental analyzer calculate?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "For any Grand Strand address you enter, it estimates property value, market rent, DSCR, cap rate, net operating income, monthly cash flow, cash-on-cash return, and appreciation, and it flags nearby permit activity."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is DSCR and why does it matter?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Debt-Service Coverage Ratio is net operating income divided by annual debt service. Investor lenders typically look for 1.20 or higher. It tells you whether the rent comfortably covers the loan."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What cap rate is realistic for a Myrtle Beach long-term rental?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "As of July 2026, a Horry County rental bought in the cheaper third of the market returns 4.2 to 7.5 percent a year after costs with a property manager, and 5.1 to 8.8 percent without one. Dividing the same rent by the typical value of every home in the area gives a much lower number, because most of those homes are not rentals. The rental returns page has the figure for each area."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Are the numbers an appraisal?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. They are an actual screening estimate to compare deals quickly. Confirm with comparable sales, inspections, and a licensed agent before making an offer."}}]}</script>
