<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only if the rent still covers the dues, and on most condos here it does not. The middle 2-bedroom condo's dues take about a quarter to half of HUD's rent, depending on the area. A condo rented by the night has different numbers.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax on a rental in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About $1,206 a year for each $100,000 of value outside city limits, and about $1,528 in the City of Myrtle Beach. A rental is taxed on 6 percent of its value, not 4, and pays the school operating tax.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is landlord insurance on a Myrtle Beach rental?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It is priced house by house, so we get you a quote on the exact home before you make an offer. Flood is a separate policy.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you run numbers on a property listed with another brokerage?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Any home on the Grand Strand, listed with any brokerage. We use the listing, the county record, nearby rentals and the association's papers.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is running the numbers free?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. There is no fee and no obligation. You can send one address or several.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD Fair Market Rents</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County 2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-37</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/tax-payer-services/real-property-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County real property tax</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County parcels</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/publications/p527" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Publication 527</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow home values</a>. Homes for sale: asking prices, counted in aggregate from the Coastal Carolinas Association of REALTORS® MLS (CCMLS). Resales: county deeds and parcel values, read by Chapter3. Estimates for a buying decision, not an appraisal or a loan quote.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Houses in Carolina Forest from above. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut a 1600 x 1200 px view from one NOAA map tile, raised the contrast and color slightly, and resized it.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/invest-run-the-numbers/carolina-forest-houses-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/invest-run-the-numbers/carolina-forest-houses-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Houses in The Parks of Carolina Forest, ZIP code 29579, from above. 3 of the 14 houses for sale that pass the 1 percent rule are in this ZIP code","caption":"Houses in The Parks of Carolina Forest, ZIP code 29579, from above. 3 of the 14 houses for sale that pass the 1 percent rule are in this ZIP code.","description":"Rows of similar houses with gray roofs, short driveways and small fenced back yards along curving streets in Carolina Forest, seen from above","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"NOAA National Geodetic Survey"},"creditText":"NOAA National Geodetic Survey, public domain","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (NOAA National Geodetic Survey)","lic